#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1362 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "FLIPPED noViolation -> violation by Fix #331 (M3-D18 / M2-D24 bucket 1, owner ruling 2026-08-22): NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm is RETIRED (Fix #330), so the machine-emitted var_exists guard this scenario used to pin no longer exists; absent = all-missing, empty(X) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports the defect on exactly the rows its other conjuncts select (1 here). If this goes SILENT again, a guard is being injected -- escalate, do not rewrite toward silence. History, before Fix #330: FRESH: DM deliberately carries no ACTARM column. ACTARMCD is populated. Predicted silent in BOTH disjuncts: disjunct 1 requires var_exists(\"ACTARM\") which is false; disjunct 2 requires empty(ACTARMCD) which is also false. Mirror of SD1361's fresh case (absent CODE there, absent DESCRIPTION here)."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ACTARMCD type=Char label="Actual Arm Code"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | B
